    "content": "<h1>Vehicle Overview</h1>\n<p>The <strong>Porsche 911 GT3 RS</strong> is engineered for maximum motorsport performance on both road and circuit:</p>\n<h3>Engine &amp; Performance Specifications</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Engine</strong>: 4.0L Naturally Aspirated Boxer-6</li>\n<li><strong>Horsepower</strong>: 518 hp @ 8,500 rpm</li>\n<li><strong>Torque</strong>: 342 lb-ft @ 6,300 rpm</li>\n<li><strong>0–60 mph</strong>: 3.0 seconds</li>\n<li><strong>Top Track Speed</strong>: 184 mph</li>\n<li><strong>Transmission</strong>: 7-speed Porsche Doppelkupplung (PDK) with paddle shifters</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Key Aerodynamic Innovations</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Central radiator concept inspired by the Le Mans-winning 911 RSR</li>\n<li>Continuously adjustable active aero elements on front wing and two-part rear wing</li>\n<li>Drag Reduction System (DRS) operated directly from the steering wheel</li>\n<li>High downforce setup generating 900+ lbs of downforce at 124 mph</li>\n</ul>\n"
